---
description: State what the system does; do not narrate limits, untested status, or what it is not
alwaysApply: true
---

# State what the system does

Write docs, comments, i18n, and prompts as operational facts: what a control does, where state lives, how to call an API, how to load / test / pack.

Do not add:

- Product caveats or “we do not guarantee” copy
- “Not yet implemented” / “this is not a todo” essays
- “Untested” / “CI doesn’t count” / “candidate / unofficial” banners
- Commercial positioning (“not for sale”, “local experiment only”, “not a product feature”)

If a sentence only narrates what the system is not, what was not tested, or what is not for sale, delete it. Keep the behavior.
